<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang={assigns[:site_lang] || "en"} {assigns[:theme_attrs] || %{}} class="scroll-smooth">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex" />
    <title>Not for you · Confluence Mirror</title>
    <link phx-track-static rel="stylesheet" href={~p"/assets/css/app.css"} />
    <style :if={assigns[:skin_css] not in [nil, ""]}>
      <%= Phoenix.HTML.raw(assigns[:skin_css]) %>
    </style>
  </head>
  <body class="flex min-h-screen items-center justify-center bg-base-100 px-4 text-base-content antialiased">
    <main class="w-full max-w-lg rounded-2xl border border-base-300/70 bg-base-100 p-8 text-center shadow-sm">
      <p class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-primary">403</p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold leading-tight">
        This mirror is not for your account
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-base-content/70">
        {assigns[:message] ||
          "You signed in successfully, but this account is not one the mirror was built for: it is not an administrator here and the sync has never seen it on the mirrored site."}
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-base-content/70">
        A mirror administrator can grant access — on the Confluence side by adding you to a group the
        mirrored spaces use, or on this side by making you an administrator.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-2">
        <a href={~p"/session"} class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm">Sign in another way</a>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-6 text-[11px] text-base-content/70">
        The mirror is read-only and mirrors one Confluence site.
      </p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
